    <statement><p>Simplify each expression as much as possible
and leave it without radicals.</p>
<p>(a) <m>\sqrt{ w^{8} x^{6} } =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>(b) <m>\sqrt[3]{ 64 w^{6} } =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>(c) <m>\sqrt{25 x^{6} y^{4} } =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>(d) <m>\sqrt{ 32 w^{7} y^{2} } \sqrt{ 2 y^{4} w^{9} } =</m>
<fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>w^{4}x^{3}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4w^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>5x^{3}y^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>8w^{8}y^{3}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert> SOLUTION </alert>



(a) <m>\sqrt{ w^{8} x^{6} } = (w^{8} x^{6})^{1/2} =
       w^{8/2} x^{6/2} = w^{4}x^{3}</m>.



(b) <m>\sqrt[3]{ 64 w^{6} } = (64 w^{6})^{1/3} = 64^{1/3} w^{6/3} =
       4w^{2}</m>.



(c) <m>\sqrt{25 x^{6} y^{4} } = (25 x^{6} y^{4})^{1/2} =
       5x^{3}y^{2}</m>.



(d) <m>\sqrt{ 32 w^{7} y^{2} } \sqrt{ 2 y^{4} w^{9} } =
       \sqrt{ (32 w^{7} y^{2})\cdot (2 y^{4} w^{9}) } =
       ( 64 w^{16} y^{6} )^{1/2} =
       8w^{8}y^{3}</m>.



</solution>
